WEBVTT

00:00:06.101 --> 00:00:11.611
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.691 --> 00:00:17.411
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.511 --> 00:00:21.101
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.201 --> 00:00:28.831
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:33.171
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.591 --> 00:00:35.051
But, with you...

00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:37.131
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:42.721
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.891 --> 00:00:47.441
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.441 --> 00:00:51.821
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.821 --> 00:00:53.401
Just to survive!

00:00:53.571 --> 00:00:55.361
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.361 --> 00:00:57.201
Take this moment...

00:00:57.201 --> 00:01:00.821
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.821 --> 00:01:03.031
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.031 --> 00:01:04.871
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.871 --> 00:01:08.581
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.581 --> 00:01:10.711
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.711 --> 00:01:12.421
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.421 --> 00:01:16.091
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.091 --> 00:01:18.261
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.261 --> 00:01:20.091
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.091 --> 00:01:24.011
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.026
There are three suspects.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.728
Moreover, they all have alibis.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:37.964
But, more importantly, the most bothersome
thing about this case is.…

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:41.268
…that it was done in a locked room.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.369
Then, you mean…

00:01:42.536 --> 00:01:47.841
Yes, as long as this trick remains unraveled,
we can’t solve this mystery.

00:01:45.841 --> 00:01:47.141
What the, isn't it easy?

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.209
The criminaI in this case is…

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.745
Oh, mom?

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:55.315
Don’t "Oh, mom?“ me. Have
you done your homework?

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.450
Not yet.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.753
Kyuu, you’re already in your
third year of junior high.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.155
Why can’t you study a little bit?

00:02:03.023 --> 00:02:04.257
Studying…

00:02:04.725 --> 00:02:06.126
I'm not so good at that…

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.495
I'm going to the supermarket.

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.530
Oh yeah, since I've solved the mystery…

00:02:11.098 --> 00:02:11.698
What?

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:13.700
…shall do the shopping?

00:02:16.303 --> 00:02:17.270
Wait, Kyuu!

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:21.608
The thing you were going to buy,
it was demiglaze sauce, wasn’t it?

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.479
He’s always like that, sheesh.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.886
There’s some beef in the refrigerator
that will expire today.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.022
So that means tonight we’ll
either have curry or stew.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:40.293
But it looked like curry.…it’s almost too easy.

00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:46.566
Be careful!

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:47.768
S-Sorry!

00:02:51.605 --> 00:02:52.305
Here.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:54.040
Geez.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:59.179
Hey, it’s short ten thousand yen!

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.814
You took it, didn’t you?

00:03:01.148 --> 00:03:02.783
No, I Wouldn’t do such a thing.

00:03:02.783 --> 00:03:03.483
Liar!

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.653
Can’t drop your guard for a moment these days.

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:09.189
I really don’t know what you’re talking about.

00:03:07.721 --> 00:03:09.022
You brat.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:09.756
What’s going on here?

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:14.161
Oh, Officer. This punk took my money.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.196
But I really didn’t.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.165
So how come it’s short?

00:03:18.465 --> 00:03:20.534
I'm telling the truth.
Well well, calm down.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:22.269
How can I calm down?

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.670
It’s my money!

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:24.871
118,000 yen.

00:03:30.811 --> 00:03:32.279
118,000 yen.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.815
That’s the amount of money
that dropped to the ground.

00:03:35.282 --> 00:03:40.120
To be exact, there are nine 10000 yen notes, five
5000 yen notes, and three 1000 yen notes.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.356
Officer, please count the money and see.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:46.593
Ah, excuse me a moment.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.395
Let’s see…

00:03:49.196 --> 00:03:50.897
It’s true. Just like you said.

00:03:52.299 --> 00:03:54.501
Then he didn’t take it.

00:03:55.869 --> 00:03:56.837
Wait a minute here!

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.406
I'm sure I just withdrew 100,000 yen.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.842
Why are there only 9 notes then?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:04.878
What are you doing?

00:04:05.512 --> 00:04:06.379
Trying to start something?

00:04:06.847 --> 00:04:07.948
No, I'm not.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.328
Here.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.697
Good thing we found it, isn’t it?

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.633
Gee, I'm really sorry about that.

00:04:26.867 --> 00:04:28.468
Seems I lost my temper.

00:04:29.436 --> 00:04:31.738
As an apology, order whatever you want.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.340
Are you sure?

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.575
Then I'll have a chocolate parfait.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:36.776
How about you?

00:04:37.444 --> 00:04:40.780
Ah, me? My mom’s cooking dinner at home, so…

00:04:41.448 --> 00:04:45.752
Your mom’s food is still your mom’s
food; I'm sure this'll be okay.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.421
Then, I'll have a chocolate parfait too.

00:04:48.555 --> 00:04:49.623
That’s the spirit.

00:04:50.357 --> 00:04:51.992
Well, I guess that’s everything.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.660
Let me repeat your order.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:55.762
Two chocolate parfaits.

00:04:56.563 --> 00:04:57.797
Will that be everything?

00:04:58.632 --> 00:04:59.666
Please wait for a moment.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.234
Thank you.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:04.404
Sorry, but I have to go from here
to the station to buy a ticket.

00:05:05.005 --> 00:05:06.206
Are you going on a trip?

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:09.376
My daughter’s wedding in Hokkaido.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.612
That’s what the money was for.

00:05:14.114 --> 00:05:16.549
Well now, I’m really sorry.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:19.586
I'll go ahead and pay the bill so take your time.

00:05:21.288 --> 00:05:22.222
He left.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:23.290
What should we do?

00:05:23.657 --> 00:05:24.758
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:25.859
Here are the chocolate parfaits.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.731
Well, since he bought this for
us, we might as well eat.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:32.632
Guess so.

00:05:34.935 --> 00:05:37.871
I'm Kyuu, third year junior high. Nice to meet you.

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:41.441
I'm Minami Magumi. I'm a third
year junior high student too.

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:43.443
Really? You’re the same age as me!

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.578
I thought you were older.

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.948
Do I look that old?

00:06:04.064 --> 00:06:04.898
Deduction?

00:06:05.332 --> 00:06:09.336
Yup, because that old man didn’t
look like he was lying.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:13.506
Moreover, there was nobody else who
could have touched the money.

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:17.477
Therefore, after the money dropped
out of the old man’s wallet…

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.112
…the notes had to fall somewhere, right?

00:06:19.913 --> 00:06:23.583
Using deduction, the only other place it could
have fallen was into the old mans umbrella.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.389
Uh, am! boring you?

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:31.124
Incredible! You’re incredible!

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.560
I see, that’s right.

00:06:34.995 --> 00:06:37.263
I’d like to do that kind of deduction too.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.200
This is the first time a girl said
something like that to me.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:46.339
Come to think of it, earlier, how did you know the
amount of money that was scattered on the ground?

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:48.074
That’s because…

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.311
Because I remembered.

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:52.879
You remembered?

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:55.015
In just that moment?

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.219
Do you know what photographic memory is?

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:00.320
What’s that?

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:04.057
If I've seen something, even for
a moment, I won’t forget it.

00:07:05.025 --> 00:07:06.993
I've had that ability since I was born.

00:07:09.863 --> 00:07:11.398
Hmm, there’s someone there…

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:12.232
Where?

00:07:12.966 --> 00:07:14.334
On top of the crane on that building.

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:17.370
What’s he doing in a place like that?

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.707
Doesn’t that look like he’s waving "bye bye“?

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:23.109
"Bye bye"? No way!

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.349
Oh no, he jumped!

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:30.517
That can’t be true!

00:07:40.393 --> 00:07:41.261
Sorry about that.

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:43.263
Hey!

00:07:44.097 --> 00:07:45.131
What’s up with them?

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:54.407
Hey!

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:57.077
Why are you guys in such a hurry?

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.845
Somebody Jumped!

00:07:59.112 --> 00:07:59.913
What did you say?

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:05.485
Hey! Hey!

00:08:11.891 --> 00:08:13.093
Call the police.

00:08:15.261 --> 00:08:15.862
It’s him.

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:17.030
Oh no!

00:08:18.698 --> 00:08:19.265
Hurry!

00:08:20.066 --> 00:08:20.934
Is this the police?

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:24.971
Yes, please.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.842
You saw saw it too?

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:30.643
Yes. Uhm?

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:33.546
Hey, looks like someone fell after all.

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:36.182
Nakaﬁma-san.

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:49.062
Yes, I caught sight of somebody falling from the crane.

00:08:49.429 --> 00:08:52.832
And so, in a panic, I called the guys in the office.

00:08:53.433 --> 00:08:58.204
I just happened to be in the office and was about to go home.

00:08:58.838 --> 00:08:59.739
Me too.

00:09:00.507 --> 00:09:03.576
Yes I was helping with the design.

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.945
That’s why I'm here doing & preliminary survey.

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:08.248
Geez, doing something like committing suicide.

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:11.217
And at our workplace of all things.

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:14.120
Old man Nakajima had been grumbling a lot.

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:16.422
Maybe he just got sick of living.

00:09:17.157 --> 00:09:17.991
Is that so?

00:09:18.491 --> 00:09:21.027
Well everyone, thank you for your cooperation.

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:22.295
Please wait a minute!

00:09:22.929 --> 00:09:25.498
I don’t believe that old man would commit suicide.

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:28.368
Oh? Why do you say that?

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:33.039
You see, we became acquainted
with him just an hour ago.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.541
We met by coincidence.

00:09:35.475 --> 00:09:39.846
That’s when he told us his daughter was
getting married in Hokkaido tomorrow.

00:09:40.013 --> 00:09:42.048
And that we was buying a ticket to go there.

00:09:42.749 --> 00:09:44.517
There’s no way he would’ve committed suicide.

00:09:46.186 --> 00:09:48.087
Hey, check it out.

00:09:48.388 --> 00:09:48.788
Yes sir.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:52.292
But if it’s not suicide…

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:55.195
D-Don’t tell me, it’s murder?

00:09:55.628 --> 00:09:57.597
Kizaki, it wasn’t you, was it?

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.399
Why would it be me?

00:09:59.799 --> 00:10:03.136
This morning you were quarreling with the old man.

00:10:03.503 --> 00:10:04.671
It was pretty heated, wasn’t it?

00:10:06.206 --> 00:10:08.107
The old man was dissing my work.

00:10:08.841 --> 00:10:10.376
But why would I kill him for that?

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:15.481
And how about you, supervisor?
Don’t you have a motive too?

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:16.049
What?

00:10:16.549 --> 00:10:20.019
You were always saying you were gonna
fire the old man, weren’t you?

00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:21.621
Now look here.

00:10:22.055 --> 00:10:24.257
I was just taking his age into consideration.

00:10:24.691 --> 00:10:26.759
I just wanted him to find some less strenuous work.

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:28.828
That doesn’t mean I'm a murderer!

00:10:29.195 --> 00:10:29.963
Calm down.

00:10:30.363 --> 00:10:31.464
Come to think of it, Kurihara-san.

00:10:32.332 --> 00:10:34.767
Why were you in the area?

00:10:35.635 --> 00:10:37.337
Like I said, I was doing a preliminary survey.

00:10:37.637 --> 00:10:38.771
At this time?

00:10:39.272 --> 00:10:40.640
That’s because…

00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:42.976
That’s right, Detective!

00:10:43.776 --> 00:10:45.945
The criminal can’t be one of us, you see?

00:10:46.279 --> 00:10:46.746
Huh?

00:10:47.146 --> 00:10:51.918
When old man Nakajima fell, it had to
take us 4 to 5 minutes to come here.

00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:54.921
But, in this building, the staircase
hasn’t been finished yet.

00:10:55.488 --> 00:11:00.627
So we have to use the elevator to
go up, but it’s absurdly slow.

00:11:01.227 --> 00:11:05.999
That’s right. The elevator takes about
10 minutes to reach the top.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.702
In other words, it couldn’t be any of us.

00:11:09.969 --> 00:11:11.671
It takes 10 minutes?

00:11:13.039 --> 00:11:13.806
Excuse me, sir.

00:11:14.574 --> 00:11:18.544
We found a ticket for the night train to
Hokkaido in the deceased’s pocket.

00:11:19.145 --> 00:11:21.547
Damn, now we can’t say it’s suicide.

00:11:22.048 --> 00:11:27.453
No, I definitely saw that old man waving his
searchlight around and around towards the sky.

00:11:28.421 --> 00:11:30.256
No matter how we look at it, it’s suicide.

00:11:31.491 --> 00:11:35.128
For now, we’ll look into both possibilities in this case.

00:11:35.828 --> 00:11:38.364
So please give us your contact information here.

00:11:39.866 --> 00:11:41.267
It wasn’t me, really!

00:11:44.704 --> 00:11:47.607
If it takes 10 minutes to come down from the roof…

00:11:47.907 --> 00:11:51.077
Then everyone here has an alibi, don’t they?

00:11:52.979 --> 00:11:53.946
Huh? Where’s Kyuu-kun?

00:11:56.616 --> 00:11:57.450
What? Over there!

00:11:57.917 --> 00:11:58.584
You there, wait!

00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:01.921
Mr. Detective, I'm going up for a bit.

00:12:02.422 --> 00:12:03.389
Come back here!

00:12:06.926 --> 00:12:08.561
It really is slow.

00:12:13.633 --> 00:12:15.401
Hey, is he going to be okay?

00:12:15.968 --> 00:12:17.537
It’s dangerous! Get back down here!

00:12:17.837 --> 00:12:19.005
Wait, Kyuu-kun.

00:12:25.111 --> 00:12:26.379
That startled me.

00:12:33.386 --> 00:12:34.020
Hey!

00:12:39.492 --> 00:12:40.460
I see!

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:41.527
What are you doing?

00:12:41.994 --> 00:12:43.429
That’s dangerous, so wait there!

00:12:46.666 --> 00:12:47.734
I understand now!

00:12:48.034 --> 00:12:48.601
Huh?

00:12:49.802 --> 00:12:52.138
This case is neither a suicide nor an accident.

00:12:53.139 --> 00:12:54.073
It’s murder!

00:12:55.174 --> 00:12:56.075
What?

00:12:57.009 --> 00:12:57.710
Murder?

00:12:58.244 --> 00:13:00.146
And the criminal is one of us here.

00:13:00.913 --> 00:13:01.914
What do you mean?

00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:03.349
I don’t understand.

00:13:04.684 --> 00:13:05.685
There are two hints.

00:13:06.452 --> 00:13:09.055
The first one is the light of the waving searchlight.

00:13:11.357 --> 00:13:14.394
The other one is a rope that’s tied around the crane.

00:13:15.461 --> 00:13:16.462
What’s that?

00:13:17.196 --> 00:13:19.098
Tell us clearly if you’re gonna be cocky about it.

00:13:19.699 --> 00:13:21.667
Unfortunately, there’s no proof yet.

00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:25.104
Mr. Detective, can you give me a little time?

00:13:25.638 --> 00:13:26.239
Time?

00:13:26.939 --> 00:13:29.542
I'll find the proof no matter what!

00:13:30.076 --> 00:13:31.577
That’s our job!

00:13:32.478 --> 00:13:34.247
That’s enough! Get back down here!

00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:45.358
We’re finished here, aren’t we, Detective?

00:13:46.793 --> 00:13:47.927
We have work to do so…

00:13:49.028 --> 00:13:51.230
Yeah, please go ahead. We’re finished.

00:13:52.298 --> 00:13:55.034
Please, let me look for the proof!

00:13:56.369 --> 00:13:57.703
I wonder what he meant.

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.071
Next person, please.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:02.041
Oh, yes.

00:14:03.543 --> 00:14:05.244
Well then, I'll be going.

00:14:05.878 --> 00:14:06.312
Fine.

00:14:06.779 --> 00:14:09.315
Do you believe what the boy said?

00:14:10.016 --> 00:14:10.817
Get real.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.919
What would I be doing taking something
a kid says seriously?

00:14:14.253 --> 00:14:16.322
But there’s something about him…

00:14:16.722 --> 00:14:17.390
Eh?

00:14:18.458 --> 00:14:21.060
Meh, never-mind. I'll be leaving soon too.

00:14:23.996 --> 00:14:24.564
Hmm?

00:14:28.468 --> 00:14:29.769
It’s something small, isn’t it?

00:14:32.004 --> 00:14:35.875
I don’t know what you’re looking for,
but you’re trying your best alone.

00:14:36.509 --> 00:14:37.577
I figure! should help you.

00:14:38.845 --> 00:14:40.313
I'll be able to see your underwear, you know.

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:41.747
Heh? Pervert!

00:14:41.814 --> 00:14:42.815
Looks like you guys are having fun.

00:14:44.984 --> 00:14:46.085
Mind if I join in too?

00:14:47.053 --> 00:14:48.387
Thank you, both of you.

00:14:49.055 --> 00:14:50.189
Eh? Where’s the detective?

00:14:50.656 --> 00:14:52.492
Detective? He wasn’t there.

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:54.727
More importantly, let’s do it!

00:14:55.394 --> 00:14:58.931
Sure, could you shine the light you got over here?

00:14:59.031 --> 00:14:59.565
Okay.

00:15:07.073 --> 00:15:08.040
A little bit ahead.

00:15:08.407 --> 00:15:09.175
Yeah, like that.

00:15:15.481 --> 00:15:16.215
There it is!

00:15:17.416 --> 00:15:18.417
You found it?

00:15:18.751 --> 00:15:19.752
What? Is it raining?

00:15:20.186 --> 00:15:21.187
Where is it?

00:15:21.721 --> 00:15:22.688
We’re going to lose it!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.468
The water’s coming from over there!

00:15:35.868 --> 00:15:36.602
Damn it.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.375
What’s with this hose?

00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:50.416
Does this mean the proof has…?

00:15:52.251 --> 00:15:53.686
Why don’t you come out now?

00:15:54.487 --> 00:15:55.955
I know what you’re hiding.

00:15:58.591 --> 00:16:00.593
You used the searchlight from
the top of the building…

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.595
…to draw attention to the jump.

00:16:04.931 --> 00:16:08.935
Everyone who rushed to the scene
would assume it was a suicide.

00:16:14.774 --> 00:16:18.411
Furthermore, by being among the eyewitnesses
rushing to the crime scene…

00:16:19.145 --> 00:16:24.150
…even if they suspect murder, the time needed
to get down from the top of the building…

00:16:24.884 --> 00:16:27.053
…would give you a solid alibi.

00:16:32.925 --> 00:16:35.328
It’s a well made alibi trick, but…

00:16:36.629 --> 00:16:40.566
The old man’s murderer is you, isn’t it?

00:16:41.033 --> 00:16:42.635
Shinoda-san!

00:16:43.102 --> 00:16:43.769
Heh?

00:16:44.137 --> 00:16:44.837
Shinoda?

00:16:45.638 --> 00:16:46.839
No, wait a minute.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.941
I don’t know what’s going on.

00:16:49.408 --> 00:16:53.513
I just don’t want the workers to come here
tomorrow and see the bloodstained earth.

00:16:53.779 --> 00:16:55.314
I just intended to wash it off.

00:16:55.615 --> 00:16:57.116
I didn’t know you were there.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:02.188
And didn’t you guys see old
man Nakajima jump too?

00:17:03.623 --> 00:17:07.693
He was on the crane, waving his searchlight
around towards the sky. And…

00:17:07.693 --> 00:17:08.561
You said it again.

00:17:08.628 --> 00:17:09.128
Eh?

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:14.867
How do you know that he was waving his
searchlight around toward the sky?

00:17:15.935 --> 00:17:17.236
This building is pretty tall…

00:17:17.803 --> 00:17:22.341
I was nearby and all I could see was
the light swinging side by side.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.746
Isn’t the reason you know the
light was waving around…

00:17:27.413 --> 00:17:29.582
…because you’re the one that was waving it?

00:17:31.284 --> 00:17:33.819
I found the remains of a rubber
rope on the tip of the crane.

00:17:34.787 --> 00:17:37.957
In other words, what we saw was not a jump.

00:17:41.694 --> 00:17:45.698
It was a bungee jump made to look like a jump!

00:17:53.573 --> 00:17:56.209
After you prepared the bungee jump…

00:17:56.676 --> 00:17:59.178
…you called Nakajima-san to
the roof and pushed him off.

00:17:59.712 --> 00:18:02.648
And then, to protect yourself from being caught…

00:18:02.848 --> 00:18:05.251
…you climbed the crane and waved the searchlight.

00:18:06.319 --> 00:18:08.421
That way, it would seem to the
people on the ground that…

00:18:08.955 --> 00:18:10.723
…you were about to commit suicide by jumping off.

00:18:12.058 --> 00:18:13.092
Then you jumped.

00:18:20.666 --> 00:18:23.803
After that, using an extra length,
you got down from the rope.

00:18:24.203 --> 00:18:25.538
And cut the rope.

00:18:26.172 --> 00:18:29.342
When you did that, without the weight,
the rubber would retract.

00:18:30.209 --> 00:18:33.412
And, tied to the crane, nobody would find this rope.

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:36.315
This mechanism should have been sufficient.

00:18:37.049 --> 00:18:38.517
Interesting story, yet…

00:18:38.851 --> 00:18:40.486
Isn’t everything’s just speculation?

00:18:40.753 --> 00:18:44.890
Yes, but earlier you heard me figure out the hints.

00:18:45.224 --> 00:18:47.426
So when you realized you left the
proof at the crime scene…

00:18:48.294 --> 00:18:49.829
…you used the hose.

00:18:50.229 --> 00:18:51.264
Isn’t that so?

00:18:52.098 --> 00:18:52.965
Proof?

00:18:53.099 --> 00:18:54.233
What are you talking about?

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:56.269
I was barely able to find it.

00:18:57.036 --> 00:19:00.873
The evidence that fell out because of
the bungee jump, a contact lens.

00:19:03.709 --> 00:19:04.677
So that’s it!

00:19:05.511 --> 00:19:07.546
When you were writing your contact information…

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.249
…one of your eyes was watery, wasn’t it?

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:14.353
It would be tough for you to write
wearing just one contact lens.

00:19:15.154 --> 00:19:20.960
When the police examine this contact
lens, they will find your DNA on it.

00:19:21.761 --> 00:19:24.930
It was a mistake not to take a brat like you seriously.

00:19:26.165 --> 00:19:28.367
Well then, give it back to me!

00:19:36.809 --> 00:19:42.114
Kendo, judo, karate, altogether 10-dan.
I, Touyama Kintarou-sama…

00:19:42.348 --> 00:19:44.116
…won’t let you get away with this!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:44.884
Incredible!

00:19:46.619 --> 00:19:47.353
Crap!

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:48.854
You think you can escape?

00:19:49.488 --> 00:19:50.056
Let’s go.

00:19:50.323 --> 00:19:50.856
Okay.

00:19:54.226 --> 00:19:54.860
Wait!

00:19:59.665 --> 00:20:00.299
Kinta!

00:20:01.167 --> 00:20:01.934
Never mind me!

00:20:01.934 --> 00:20:02.668
Keep going!

00:20:04.303 --> 00:20:05.037
Shit!

00:20:07.106 --> 00:20:08.074
Wait!

00:20:11.711 --> 00:20:12.378
Watch out!

00:20:13.579 --> 00:20:14.647
Out of my way!

00:20:17.883 --> 00:20:19.785
Ouch ouch ouch, s-s-stop it.

00:20:19.785 --> 00:20:20.553
Shinoda-san.

00:20:21.087 --> 00:20:26.826
You used your supervisor’s position to embezzle
money for your own private use.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.262
Nakajima-san told the truth to the owner.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:31.530
Isn’t that so?

00:20:31.964 --> 00:20:33.265
I won’t forgive him!

00:20:33.632 --> 00:20:37.336
That self-righteous old Nakajima betrayed me!

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:41.640
Don’t mess with me! Thanks to you, I might be fired!

00:20:46.545 --> 00:20:48.447
Just that is why you killed the old man?

00:20:49.582 --> 00:20:51.884
Inspector Arai, please take care of the rest.

00:20:56.155 --> 00:20:57.523
Ah, Mr. Detective.

00:20:58.257 --> 00:20:59.859
Hey there, come quietly!

00:21:01.994 --> 00:21:06.065
Shinoda Hitoshi, you’re under arrest for
the murder of Nakajima Yashica-san.

00:21:07.733 --> 00:21:09.034
Alright, take him away.

00:21:09.235 --> 00:21:09.668
Yes, sir.

00:21:13.973 --> 00:21:15.875
Thank you for your assistance.

00:21:16.842 --> 00:21:17.877
Thank you also.

00:21:18.377 --> 00:21:19.278
If you'll excuse me…

00:21:23.015 --> 00:21:26.986
Because of you guys we have wrapped
this case safety, thank you.

00:21:27.386 --> 00:21:28.888
Erm, who are you?

00:21:29.321 --> 00:21:30.756
Ah, sorry.

00:21:31.524 --> 00:21:36.162
I'm actually a detective hired by the owner of
this building for an undercover investigation.

00:21:36.662 --> 00:21:39.365
My name is Katagiri Shine, a teacher at DDS.

00:21:39.965 --> 00:21:40.900
DDS?

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.635
So that’s why the detective…

00:21:42.968 --> 00:21:44.470
What is "DDS"?

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:46.472
You don’t know about it?

00:21:47.039 --> 00:21:47.573
Nope.

00:21:49.708 --> 00:21:52.812
Dan Detective School, in short, DDS.

00:21:53.646 --> 00:21:56.582
It’s the one school in Japan where students
are allowed to bear arms.

00:21:56.749 --> 00:22:00.853
It’s the detective academy founded by the
legendary detective, Dan Morihiko.

00:22:02.455 --> 00:22:03.656
Detective academy?

00:22:04.423 --> 00:22:07.827
DDS even often assists the
police on important cases.

00:22:08.394 --> 00:22:11.931
It’s students have even helped with some
of the most difficult cases of our time.

00:22:12.598 --> 00:22:14.900
Why do you guys know about it?

00:22:15.367 --> 00:22:18.103
Because I'm aiming to attend DDS!
Because I'm aiming to attend DDS!

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:19.038
Huh?
Huh?

00:22:19.672 --> 00:22:23.476
Wow, there’s really a school like that?

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:25.678
I'm definitely going there too!

00:22:26.912 --> 00:22:30.216
Hey, you don’t really get it, do you?

00:22:30.416 --> 00:22:31.317
That’s right.

00:22:31.383 --> 00:22:33.953
Attending DDS isn’t that easy, you know?

00:22:34.386 --> 00:22:35.054
Why?

00:22:35.321 --> 00:22:36.522
Because!

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:39.792
Then I'll give you this present.

00:22:42.661 --> 00:22:43.996
What’s this?

00:22:44.530 --> 00:22:47.733
This is the list of the requirements
for the examination next week.

00:22:48.501 --> 00:22:50.269
For DDS, of course.

00:22:51.237 --> 00:22:52.271
DDS!

00:22:52.805 --> 00:22:53.739
Entrance exam!

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:55.574
Please take it.

00:22:56.308 --> 00:22:58.644
Who knows, you might be accepted.

00:23:03.115 --> 00:23:04.550
I ’m back.

00:23:06.719 --> 00:23:09.021
What time do you think it is now?

00:23:11.824 --> 00:23:13.025
Sorry.

00:23:13.692 --> 00:23:15.027
There’s no dinner.

00:23:15.895 --> 00:23:16.862
Good night.

00:23:17.897 --> 00:23:18.364
Mom!

00:23:19.064 --> 00:23:20.032
What?

00:23:20.432 --> 00:23:22.735
I didn’t have dinner either.

00:23:22.735 --> 00:23:23.702
I've decided!

00:23:24.937 --> 00:23:26.338
To attend DDS!

00:23:27.273 --> 00:23:27.840
Eh?

00:23:28.474 --> 00:23:29.241
Eh?!

00:23:29.808 --> 00:23:32.711
And then I'll become the world’s best detective!

00:23:36.388 --> 00:23:46.638
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:50.028 --> 00:24:01.238
Saying "I'll always be beside you" without saying a single word.

00:24:01.478 --> 00:24:08.568
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:08.568 --> 00:24:14.198
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:14.398 --> 00:24:20.308
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:20.408 --> 00:24:25.858
I will see you off.

00:24:26.108 --> 00:24:35.298
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:37.001 --> 00:24:40.604
The legendary detective Dan Morihiko’s
detective academy, DDS.

00:24:41.172 --> 00:24:41.906
Incredible!

00:24:42.173 --> 00:24:45.042
I'll attend that school and become
the world’s best detective.

00:24:45.609 --> 00:24:49.213
In the first exam, the victim left a dying message
in the one photograph that he took!

00:24:49.513 --> 00:24:52.783
From the six suspects, will I be able to find the truth?

00:24:53.084 --> 00:24:54.185
There’s only one answer.

00:24:58.990 --> 00:25:00.691
Yes, it’s me.

00:25:02.393 --> 00:25:03.361
That’s my intention.

00:25:09.033 --> 00:25:10.334
DDS eh?
